      "title": "Trump says US will ‘hit Iran hard’ as hostilities resume – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/aug/31/us-iran-israel-hormuz-oil-donald-trump-larak-kharg-island-uae-jordan-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>Iran responded to an assault on its Larak Island by targeting US bases in Jordan</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/31/trump-threatens-further-action-us-iran-exchange-fire\">Trump threatens further action as US and Iran exchange fire in new flare-up</a></p></li></ul><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/aug/31/us-iran-israel-hormuz-oil-donald-trump-larak-kharg-island-uae-jordan-latest-news-updates?page=with%3Ablock-6a9543438f08187a5f76fcce#block-6a9543438f08187a5f76fcce\">Coinciding with this week’s G20 meeting</a>, the EU has issued a statement saying it will work with the US and other allied countries to maintain economic pressure against Iran.</p><p>“The ‌EU welcomes efforts at ensuring that Iran ceases its destabilising activities and engages in peace negotiations with good ‌faith, also through additional economic pressure, including through ​the US-led Operation Economic Outcast,” it said in reference to the pressure strategy the White House describes as “an unprecedented campaign to sever every remaining economic lifeline sustaining” the Islamic republic.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/aug/31/us-iran-israel-hormuz-oil-donald-trump-larak-kharg-island-uae-jordan-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-31T17:17:13"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump threatens further action as US and Iran exchange fire in new flare-up",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/31/trump-threatens-further-action-us-iran-exchange-fire",
      "description": "<p>Washington says it acted after observing Iran was planning to deploy fresh mines in strait of Hormuz</p><p>The US and Iran have exchanged fire for the first time in a month, with missiles and drones fired at Iranian rocket launchers on an island in the strait of Hormuz, and Iran targeting US military bases in Jordan and the United Arab Emirates in response.</p><p>The US president, Donald Trump, on Monday threatened further action. The US is to trying to prise open Tehran’s grip on shipping going through the strait, which before the war accounted for a fifth of the world’s seaborne energy supply. Washington claimed that Iranian control over the waterway had been loosened by repeated US attacks on Iranian missile launchers and radars.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/31/trump-threatens-further-action-us-iran-exchange-fire\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-31T17:13:55"
    },
    {
      "title": "UAE intercepts Iranian drone over territorial waters after US strikes",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/uae-intercepts-iranian-drone-over-territorial-waters-after-us-strikes-126083100557_1.html",
      "description": "The United Arab Emirates' air force intercepted an Iranian drone over its territorial waters Monday, the Defense Ministry said, an attack that comes after the US and Iran exchanged fire on the weekend, the first significant military action in a month.\nIn a short statement, the Defence Ministry said it \"dealt with\" an Iranian drone that was detected over its waters approaching from Iran.\nThere were no immediate claims of responsibility from Tehran nor any reports of damage. The UAE Defence Ministry later issued a second statement denying the Al Menhad Air Base in Dubai had been targeted by Iranian missiles, as had been reported by Iranian media outlets.\nThe incident came after US forces on Sunday struck Iranian rocket launchers on an Iranian island, breaking a lull in fighting in the war that has lasted more than six months.\nIran responded by launching missiles at US sites in Jordan, which were intercepted.\nEarly Monday, Iran's Foreign Ministry said that Iran would \"not hesitate to",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-31T09:36:15"
    },
    {
      "title": "US strikes Iranian rocket launchers in first military action in weeks",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/us-strikes-iranian-rocket-launchers-in-first-military-action-in-weeks-126083100048_1.html",
      "description": "US forces struck Iranian rocket launchers on the Strait of Hormuz in their first military action in a month on Sunday, breaking a lull in fighting during an intermittent war that has lasted more than six months. Iran swiftly vowed to retaliate for what it called a deadly attack.\nForces with the Revolutionary Guard Corps were observed preparing to launch rockets with sea mines into the strait, according to Tim Hawkins, a spokesperson for the US Central Command. The US military last week completed clearing sea mines from the strait's international shipping routes.\nSemiofficial news outlets in Iran reported sounds of explosions near Larak island on the strait. The Guard in a statement carried by Iran's state broadcaster noted \"the martyrdom and injury of several of our fighters and compatriots.\"\nA return to open conflict would be dangerous for the region, where Iran has targeted US military bases and infrastructure in Gulf countries since the war began on February 28.\nThe last time th",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-31T02:10:13"
    }
  ]
